---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
import { breadcrumbs, graph } from '../lib/schema';

const updated = '21 November 2026';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy policy', path: '/privacy/' },
];
const analytics = Boolean(SITE.cfAnalyticsToken);
const form = Boolean(SITE.web3formsKey);
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How aiforresearch.eu handles personal data under the GDPR: no cookies, minimal server logs, cookieless statistics and a contact form."
  schema={graph(breadcrumbs(crumbs))}
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy policy" lead={`Last updated: ${updated}`} crumbs={crumbs} />

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container--narrow prose">
      <p>
        This policy explains which personal data aiforresearch.eu ("the site") processes, why, and what rights you have under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (Regulation (EU) 2016/679, "GDPR") and the Italian Personal Data Protection Code (Legislative Decree 196/2003).
      </p>

      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The site sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser.</li>
        <li>There are no accounts, no logins, no advertising and no social media trackers.</li>
        <li>Fonts and scripts are served from our own domain, so loading a page does not contact Google or other third parties{analytics ? ', apart from the cookieless statistics described below' : ''}.</li>
        <li>We only receive your name, email address and message if you choose to contact us.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.owner.name}, {SITE.owner.city}, {SITE.owner.country}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
      </p>
      <p>No Data Protection Officer has been appointed, as the GDPR does not require one for this site.</p>

      <h2>2. Visiting the site: hosting and server logs</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted by Render Services, Inc. (San Francisco, USA). When you open a page, your browser sends technical data to the hosting servers: IP address, date and time, requested page, referring page, browser type and operating system. This is needed to deliver the page and to protect the site against abuse and attacks.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> legitimate interest in running a secure website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li>
        <li><strong>Retention:</strong> logs are kept by the host for a short period for security purposes and then deleted.</li>
        <li><strong>Transfer outside the EU:</strong> Render is based in the United States. Transfers rely on the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework where the provider is certified, or on the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses (Art. 46 GDPR).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Visitor statistics</h2>
      {analytics ? (
        <>
          <p>
            We use Cloudflare Web Analytics (Cloudflare, Inc., USA) to count page views. It sets no cookies, uses no local storage and does not build profiles or fingerprint visitors. It records the page visited, the referring site, the browser type and the country, which Cloudflare derives from your IP address without storing the address for analytics.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> legitimate interest in knowing which content is read (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li>
            <li><strong>Transfer outside the EU:</strong> EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and Standard Contractual Clauses.</li>
            <li>You can block the statistics script with any content blocker without losing any function of the site.</li>
          </ul>
        </>
      ) : (
        <p>The site currently collects no visitor statistics. If cookieless statistics are enabled in future, this section will be updated before they go live.</p>
      )}

      <h2>4. Contacting us</h2>
      <p>
        If you write to us, by email{form ? ' or through the contact form' : ''}, we process your name, email address and the content of your message to reply to you.
        {form && ' The contact form is delivered through Web3Forms (web3forms.com), which forwards the message to our mailbox and does not use it for other purposes.'}
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Legal basis:</strong> steps you request before a possible contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) or our legitimate interest in answering enquiries (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). For "tell me when the services open" requests, your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR), which you can withdraw at any time by email.</li>
        <li><strong>Retention:</strong> as long as needed to handle your request, and no longer than 24 months after the last exchange, unless a longer period is required by law.</li>
        <li><strong>Please do not send</strong> confidential proposal text or special categories of data (health, political opinions and similar) through the form.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>
        The site uses no cookies, no local storage and no tracking pixels, so no cookie banner is needed. Links to other websites (for example the sources quoted in the digest) take you to sites with their own privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>6. AI-generated content</h2>
      <p>
        The weekly digest is written by an AI model from public news feeds. No personal data of visitors is sent to the AI model, and the site makes no automated decisions about you within the meaning of Art. 22 GDPR. See the <a href="/ai-transparency/">AI transparency page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Who receives your data</h2>
      <p>
        Only the providers named above (hosting{analytics ? ', statistics' : ''}{form ? ', form delivery' : ''} and our email provider), acting on our behalf as data processors. We do not sell or rent personal data and do not share it for marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under Articles 15 to 21 GDPR you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li>have it corrected or deleted;</li>
        <li>restrict or object to its processing;</li>
        <li>receive it in a portable format;</li>
        <li>withdraw consent at any time, without affecting earlier processing.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Send requests to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We answer within one month. You can also lodge a complaint with the Italian data protection authority, the <a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it" rel="noopener">Garante per la protezione dei dati personali</a>, or with the authority in the EU country where you live or work.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Security</h2>
      <p>
        The site is static: there is no database, no login and no server-side code that stores visitor data. All traffic uses HTTPS with HSTS, and the site sends a strict Content Security Policy.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes</h2>
      <p>We will update this page if the way we handle data changes, and change the date at the top.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
